  "summary": "The Alameda County Board of Supervisors approved a 10-year contract with Flock Safety for two drone docking stations to support the Sheriff's Office's Drone as First Responder program. The article discusses privacy concerns about expanding aerial surveillance, references Flock's ALPR controversies, and cites a Sonoma County ACLU lawsuit over drone misuse. Alameda County policy requires drone data be deleted within 60 days unless tied to an investigation.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The Alameda County Board of Supervisors on Tuesday approved a 10-year contract for two drone docking stations for Flock Safety's Drone as First Responder program for the Alameda County Sheriff's Office",
